ef=\"/search?topic=interpretability\">View more<span class=\"f9ZZrG_icon\"><svg width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"currentColor\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"flex-shrink:0\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M11.1465 4.64648C11.3417 4.45127 11.6582 4.45136 11.8535 4.64648L16.8535 9.64649L16.916 9.72267C16.9703 9.80418 17 9.90061 17 10C17 10.1326 16.9473 10.2598 16.8535 10.3535L11.8535 15.3535C11.6583 15.5486 11.3417 15.5487 11.1465 15.3535C10.9513 15.1583 10.9514 14.8418 11.1465 14.6465L15.293 10.5H3.5C3.2239 10.5 3.00006 10.2761 3 10C3 9.72387 3.22386 9.50001 3.5 9.50001H15.293L11.1465 5.35352C10.9514 5.15826 10.9513 4.8417 11.1465 4.64648Z\"></path></svg></span></a></div></aside></div><div class=\"PA4F1q_body\" data-article-body=\"true\" data-theme=\"ivory\"><p class=\"PA4F1q_reading-column post-text\">At the link above, we report some developing work from the Anthropic Interpretability team on Crosscoder Model Diffing, which might be of interest to researchers working actively in this space. </p><p class=\"PA4F1q_reading-column post-text\">As ever, we'd ask readers to treat these results like those of a colleague sharing some thoughts or preliminary experiments for a few minutes at a lab meeting, rather than a mature paper.</p></div></div></article></div><!--$--><!--/$-->","canvases":0}